  data:  # abe8
    kind: work_item  # abe8
    title: "Symbol.canonical_name docstring oversells the field; clarify it's set only when 'name' is unqualified"  # abe8
    status: todo_hard  # abe8
    priority: 4  # abe8
    parent:  # abe8
    tags:  # abe8
    - self_analysis  # abe8
    - dogfooding  # abe8
    - docs  # abe8
    isbefore: []  # abe8
    duplicate_of: []  # abe8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # abe8
    pr_ref:  # abe8
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 7).**\n\n**Symptom.** IR docstring at `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:226` says:\n\n```\ncanonical_name: Fully qualified name (e.g., 'mymodule.MyClass.method')\n```\n\nBut the actual field population on hypergumbo's self-analysis:\n\n| Kind | With canonical_name | Without |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| method | 0 | 17,412 |\n| function | 0 | 6,133 |\n| class | 0 | 4,241 |\n| variable | 0 | 1,487 |\n| module | 0 | 385 |\n| external_symbol (synthesized) | 1,561 | 0 |\n| dependency | 81 | 0 |\n\nMainstream analyzers (Python, JS/TS, Go, Rust, Java, C++, Ruby) leave `canonical_name=None`. Only 10 niche-language analyzers (nix, r_lang, hlsl, asm, capnp, ada, fish, verilog, powershell, css) and 2 linkers (yjs_crdt, wasm_bindgen) actively set it. The only other producer is `ir.py:1048` for synthesized external boundary nodes.\n\n**Subagent verification (round 7) of containment.py impact:**\n\n- 18,022 containment-linker edges produced on hypergumbo's self-analysis\n- Breakdown by `meta.evidence_type`: `naming_convention=17,413` (96.6%), `span_overlap=609` (3.4%), `canonical_name=0`\n- The canonical_name code paths at `containment.py:204-205` and `:266-268` short-circuit for every mainstream-analyzer symbol\n- Phase 1 (naming_convention) and Phase 2 (span_overlap) carry the load with zero coverage loss\n- **No production path silently fails** when canonical_name is None\n\n**Why this is correct-by-construction (not a bug):**\n\nFor Python/JS/Go/Rust/Java/C++/Ruby, `sym.name` is already `\"ClassName.methodName\"` style — the parent path is already encoded in the name. Adding `canonical_name = \"module.ClassName.methodName\"` would duplicate information. The field is genuinely useful for niche languages where `sym.name=\"rpc_method\"` is unqualified but the containing service is known structurally — e.g., proto RPCs, nested capnp messages.\n\n**Fix proposal — docstring update only.**\n\nEdit `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py` line ~226, replacing:\n\n```python\ncanonical_name: Fully qualified name (e.g., 'mymodule.MyClass.method')\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```python\ncanonical_name: Set only when `name` is unqualified but a fully-qualified path\n    is known (e.g., proto RPCs, nested capnp messages). For mainstream-analyzer\n    languages where `name` already encodes the parent (Python's\n    \"ClassName.method\", Java's \"Class.method\"), this field is deliberately\n    None. Consumers needing fully-qualified identifiers should fall back to\n    `name` for those cases. Set by niche-language analyzers (nix, r_lang,\n    hlsl, asm, capnp, ada, fish, verilog, powershell, css), the yjs_crdt and\n    wasm_bindgen linkers, and the external-boundary synthesis path in ir.py.\n```\n\nAlso add a one-line clarification to `linkers/containment.py:20-24` module docstring noting that the canonical_name code paths are reachable for niche languages but mainstream analyzers deliberately leave the field None (containment falls through to naming_convention / span_overlap).\n\n**Severity.** Low — documentation drift. No code change needed. Catches the next person to read the IR docstring or evaluate canonical_name as a disambiguation key (e.g., as I did when filing INV-fusus / R4-1 stable_id collisions, where I suggested joining on (stable_id, canonical_name) as a fix — that suggestion would have been ineffective in practice since canonical_name is None for the colliding symbols).\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:204-359` — Symbol docstring (line 226 is the canonical_name claim)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/containment.py:20-24, 200-270` — consumer-side\n- `WI-fozoh-…` (done) — closed the inverse case (null canonical_name on EXTERNAL boundary nodes was the bug; this case has null on internal source nodes and that's deliberate)\n- `INV-fusus-…` (filed round 4) — stable_id collision item that referenced canonical_name as a possible disambiguation; this finding should refine that suggestion\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 7 section."  # abe8
    fields: {}  # abe8
